        "Description": "The Raccoon (Procyon lotor) is a native mammal found year-round, at times observed in tree branches during the summer months at Great Falls Park, Virginia. While predominantly nocturnal and most active from dusk to dawn, raccoons are occasionally seen during the day. These adaptable omnivores thrive throughout the park's deciduous hardwood forests and river floodplain habitats.",
