      "id": "land-regular-36-01",
      "identityNameBase": "Mira Mask",
      "characterId": "mira-mask",
      "fullSpecies": "Procyon lotor",
      "platform": "facebook",
      "contentType": "post",
      "title": "What my paws were doing",
      "status": "candidate",
      "independentLeadReview": "pending",
      "prose": "Woke with claws pressing into my palm. Pulled away and the pressure followed. My other paw had hold of this one.\n\nI opened the first paw. The second tightened. Opened that one and nearly rolled off the branch trying to see what the first was doing.\n\nPut my cheek back on the bark. Set one paw down, then the other. Waited until both had stopped gripping.\n\nThey crept together again as I got sleepy. I let them, with the claws out of the way.",
      "altText": "A raccoon lies sideways in a tree fork, cheek against bark and its forepaws gathered together in front of its face.",
      "fictionBoundary": "Self-contact and branch support are visible. Sleep, pressure, sequential unclenching, a slight roll and gentler contact are invented. The paws are not identified as a caught hind foot. Source sex and precise age are unrecorded; female narrator is established fiction. No diagnostic confusion, injury or universal raccoon behavior claimed.",
      "visualReview": "Exact original individually opened before prose; no crop, upscale or generated image.",
      "sexAgeEvidence": "Self-contact and branch support are visible. Sleep, pressure, sequential unclenching, a slight roll and gentler contact are invented. The paws are not identified as a caught hind foot. Source sex and precise age are unrecorded; female narrator is established fiction. No diagnostic confusion, injury or universal raccoon behavior claimed."
