      "id": "land-regular-36-02",
      "identityNameBase": "Oswin Broadback",
      "characterId": "oswin-broadback",
      "fullSpecies": "Bison bison",
      "platform": "facebook",
      "contentType": "post",
      "title": "Where I put my weight",
      "status": "candidate",
      "independentLeadReview": "pending",
      "prose": "He pushed my head sideways until I could see grass with one eye and nothing but him with the other.\n\nI drove harder. My back feet dug in. My front feet slid.\n\nHad to stop trying to move him long enough to move one foot of my own. Set it farther out. Felt the ground hold. Brought my head back against his and pushed from there.\n\nWe turned a little. Neither of us went backward. I could feel him breathing through the hair against my forehead.\n\nWhen we parted, I stood with my feet still spread. He stood that way too.",
      "altText": "Two adult bison bulls press lowered heads together in grass; the left bull has one eye visible, with other bison behind.",
      "fictionBoundary": "Adult bulls and head contact are source-supported. Foot slipping, adjustment, mutual turning, breathing sensations and aftermath are invented. No winner, mating outcome, injury, trapped horns or audience reaction is asserted. Source location Wind Cave illustrates compatible grassland without relocating the fictional Yellowstone home.",
      "visualReview": "Exact original individually opened before prose; no crop, upscale or generated image.",
      "sexAgeEvidence": "Adult bulls and head contact are source-supported. Foot slipping, adjustment, mutual turning, breathing sensations and aftermath are invented. No winner, mating outcome, injury, trapped horns or audience reaction is asserted. Source location Wind Cave illustrates compatible grassland without relocating the fictional Yellowstone home."
